@startuml
' The team lifecycle, the two states from which an action became unreachable (D3),
' and the divergence between chain and PDS that no code reconciles (D4).
title Agent-team lifecycle — the unreachable actions (D3) and the divergent state (D4)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #455A64
skinparam state {
  BorderThickness 1.5
  FontColor #263238
}

[*] --> Draft

state Draft #ECEFF1 {
  Draft : no registry URI
  Draft : primary button reads **Deploy**
}

state Deployed #E8F5E9 {
  Deployed : ""uri = rho:id:…"" recorded on chain
  Deployed : Run works
  Deployed : primary button reads **Run**
}

state Edited #FFF3E0 {
  Edited : ""hasGraphChanges = true""
  Edited : primary button reads **Deploy** again
}

state Published #E8F5E9 {
  Published : PDS account ""@handle"" exists
  Published : ""com.f1r3sky.agentsteam.config"" (rkey ""self"") → URI
  Published : an @mention triggers a run
}

state "Divergent\n(chain says published, PDS has no account)" as Divergent #FFEBEE {
  Divergent : publish record survives on chain
  Divergent : the account it names is gone
  Divergent : UI still presents the team as published
}

Draft --> Deployed : Deploy
Deployed --> Edited : edit the graph
Edited --> Deployed : Deploy
Deployed --> Published : Publish\n<size:10>creates the PDS account</size>
Published --> Deployed : re-deploy\n<size:10>mints a **new** URI; the config</size>\n<size:10>record still names the old one</size>

Published --> Divergent : ""stack.sh backend"" cold start\n<size:10>pg_clear + valkey flush</size>
Divergent --> Published : publish again\n<size:10>the only exit — and it worked</size>\n<size:10>only because the wipe also</size>\n<size:10>freed the handle</size>

note right of Deployed #FFF3E0
  **D3 — the gap.** The primary button can
  offer one action, so on a deployed team
  with no pending edits it reads Run, and
  both re-deploying and publishing had no
  entry point in the editor at all.
  Publishing lived only on the dashboard
  card; re-deploying required making an
  edit first.

  Fixed by the caret menu (""dc3076a""),
  gated on ""isDeployed"" — the precondition
  both actions share.
end note

note right of Divergent #FFEBEE
  **D4 — no reconciliation.** Two systems
  hold one fact and nothing compares them.
  Diagnosis: ""com.atproto.sync.listRepos""
  on :2583 returns only the three dev-env
  defaults, so a published team should
  appear as a fourth repo.

  **Closed by** ""ed79aaa"": the publication
  records its handle and DID, and
  ""GET …/published"" consults the PDS
  rather than trusting the chain alone.

  **And a correction.** "Publish again" was
  the prescribed exit, but publishing always
  called ""create_account"", so it succeeded
  here *only* because the wipe had also freed
  the handle. Anywhere else it died on
  ""400 Handle already taken"". Fixed in
  ""d938999""; see figure 9.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#E8F5E9>| healthy state |
  |<#FFF3E0>| healthy, but an action is unreachable |
  |<#FFEBEE>| inconsistent across systems |
  |<#ECEFF1>| initial |
endlegend
@enduml
